}}|caption=[[Cladogram]] showing the [[phylogeny]] and relationships of ''H.&nbsp;foliosum'' within the "''Androsaemum''-group" based on Meseguer et al. 2013{{sfn|Meseguer|Aldasoro|Sanmartín|2013|p=386}}|align=left}}The species was first formally described as Hypericum foliosum in 1789 in the botanical journal Hortus Kewensis by William Aiton. In this original description, based on the type specimen collected on São Miguel in 1777, Aiton noted the species' long petals and sharp calyx as differentiating characteristics. Augustin Pyramus de Candolle followed Aiton's nomenclature in 1824, as did several other authors through the 19th century.
